The props of the App component differ from the props of a page component, so it makes sense to not set the page component's props to the App's props by default.

This fixes the issue when we create a HOC for the App component:
```
import AppComponent from 'next/app';

export const wrapTheApp = (App: typeof AppComponent) => {
  const someHoc = (props: AppProps) => {
    return <App {...props} />;
  };
  return someHoc;
};
```
and get a very cryptic error saying that the App's `Component` prop doesn't match the `Component` prop of the `props` object.

